# ── Development-process resources: kept OUT of the published repo ─────────────
# Internal, normative source-of-truth specs and planning notes written during
# development. Not part of the public product surface — the public story is told
# by docs/ (served on GitHub Pages) and, later, a separate distilled
# "development theory" write-up. Excluding them keeps the raw dev process private
# when the repo is published.
/sots/
/plan/

# build outputs
/bin/
*.exe
/web/detector.wasm
/docs/report.html

# ACME/autocert on-disk cache (issued certs + account key; engine -acme-cache)
/acme-cache/

# e2e artifacts
/test/node_modules/
/test/e2e/results.json
/test/shoot.mjs
# NOTE: test/package-lock.json is intentionally COMMITTED (SoT-31 R8) so `npm ci`
# in the red image / CI is deterministic — do not ignore it.

# jekyll / github pages local build (the site is built by GitHub, never committed)
/docs/_site/
/docs/.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata

# local / secrets
*.log
*.local
.env
*.pem
*.key
/var/

# os / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker Red/Blue run artifacts (keep the dir, ignore outputs)
/deployments/artifacts/*
!/deployments/artifacts/.gitkeep
